extends RefCounted

## Shared Medieval rules plus only the selected difficulty's mechanics.
const COMMON: String = "CONTROLS\n• Spectator mode beside difficulty launches four AI armies with no player; use camera controls to watch. Spectator maps repeat the same tile positions and types at 90-degree turns in all four quadrants, giving each corner the same objective distances; total tile count still varies. The fast-forward icon cycles 1x → 2x → 4x → 8x → 1x in any Medieval match; every new match starts at 1x.\n• L-click or drag a box to select; click a tile to move or an enemy to focus.\n• R-click drag / Space-drag: pan · Wheel: zoom · A: select all · Esc: pause\n\nCAPTURE & HEAL\n• Only seated warriors capture spades/hearts/eligible bases; more allies capture faster. Any living opponent in the tile pauses all capture progress, including moving or fighting opponents. Progress resumes when uncontested; friendly units do not block each other.\n• Human capture times: 1/2/3/4/5 seated warriors take 14/7/3.5/2/1 seconds. Each additional seated Human reduces that time by another 10% (6: 0.9s, 7: 0.81s), without a scaling cap. Other races: 16.7 seconds divided by seated warriors.\n• Partial capture progress stays when you leave. Original bases require their original race to be eliminated. Conquered bases can be recaptured while their current owner lives.\n• Each captured enemy base adds 6 capacity; losing it removes that bonus. Spawn speed stays unchanged. Spawns alternate across owned bases in order.\n• Owned spades speed spawning; for demons, owned hearts provide the same spawning boost. Owned hearts and bases heal seated warriors at 1.8 HP/sec; demons heal only at bases, never hearts.\n• Elves heal at 3.6 HP/sec on owned hearts; base healing is unchanged. Elves must be sitting and unattacked for 3 seconds to heal. On every difficulty, enemy elves below 30% HP seek the nearest owned heart/base without a distance limit, move 30% slower until arrival, and recover to full HP. Retreat travel stops after 20 seconds if no healing tile is reached. Seated healing is not subject to this travel timeout. Retreat cooldown is 30 seconds from arrival or the 20-second travel deadline. Healing elves interrupt recovery to pursue attackers under the shared retaliation rule; fighting never heals. Threatened tile defenders can randomly fight or retreat if cooldown permits; fighting commits for 3 seconds.\n\nSPAWNING & COMBAT\n• Universal AI retaliation: every race and difficulty responds to attack attempts from any distance, including misses. Exception: retreating Humans, Orcs and Elves ignore ranged attackers and continue to safety; retreating allies are not recruited into ranged responses. Allies within 8 movement cells join the victim. Pursue and fight until the attacker dies or stops attacking for 3 seconds. This takes precedence over all strategic and recovery orders; suspended recovery resumes afterward.\n• All races on every difficulty may share routes and objectives with other friendly squads. Coincidental crowds are allowed; no group repulsion or destination-separation penalty applies. Unit cell occupancy still applies. Pursuers use ordinary individual movement without shared attack-position reservations.\n• Human AI: individual orders on Easy; Elf-style squads on Normal/Expert. Below 30% HP, retreat to the nearest owned healing tile within 20 Manhattan cells, else nearest owned base, and stay until full HP. Full recovery starts a 20-second cooldown; travel has no timeout that cancels recovery. On an owned heart with wounded Humans, all Human occupants wait together, including healthy companions, until everyone is fully healed. Earlier-healed members keep waiting; the group then leaves toward one shared objective. This applies even above 30% HP or during cooldown. Available Humans intercept enemies within current attack range. No numerical engagement restriction or conquest waves.\n• Enemy proximity reactions run every simulation tick on every difficulty, including during movement. Humans intercept within their current reach while available. Elves attack any moving or stationary enemy within their reach, except during healing recovery when they only retaliate. Demons detect enemies within 3 cells and pursue their chosen target until death. They attack adjacent hostile blockers before resuming the original pursuit.\n• Orcs spawn twice as fast. All races start with 12 capacity.\n• Orcs gain +1 capacity per two owned spades or hearts. Converted orcs are shown as (+N) and do not consume spawn capacity.\n• Melee warriors approach enemies individually; upgraded humans and elves can attack from farther away.\n• Ranged attacks (reach above 1 cell): 80% hit chance against stationary targets. Moving targets: compare attacker swings/sec to target movement multiplier; faster/equal/slower gives 70%/50%/30%. Melee: 90% against stationary targets; cannot hit moving targets except elves, who can attack moving enemies at any reach.\n• Engaged orcs on one victim receive +0/+1/+2/+3 group punch in stable attacker order: regular orcs deal 2/3/4/5 punch. Converted orcs participate normally; their final punch remains capped at 10.\n• Humans: kills repeat +2 max HP, +2 punch, then +2 attack reach, scaling without a tier cap. Human assists independently repeat +1 max HP, +1 permanent punch, then +1 reach, without a cap; deal damage within 5 seconds before death to qualify once per victim. The killer receives only its kill upgrade. Humans hit one target per swing. Fighting on owned tiles grants +1 punch, lasting 3 seconds after leaving.\n• Orc killing blows: 25/50/75/100% conversion chance for 1/2/3/4+ successful hit stacks on the victim in the last 5 seconds; repeated hits by the same orc each add a stack, even above capacity. Converted orcs inherit maximum HP up to 30 and permanent punch up to 10 and spawn at that capped full HP; they use orc group damage, with final punch still capped at 10; reach resets to 1 cell. Temporary bonuses are not inherited.\n• Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds. Reach costs 2/3/4 bonus HP per extra cell: +2 HP each to reach 3 cells, then +3 HP each to reach 5 cells, then +4 HP each forever. Owned tiles grant no punch bonus.\n• Demons: +1 punch per kill; 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds. Demon killers heal 2 HP; assists never heal. Healing is capped at max HP; killers do not also receive assist healing. Enemy demons never retreat to heal. At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.\n• Assist credit is once per death; HP bonuses do not instantly heal. Bonuses reset on respawn. Eliminate all opponents to win.\n• Assigned units clear enemies on their ordered tile together without chasing outside it. Increased-range units can stop before entering and fire at enemies on that tile as soon as they are in reach. Once clear, stand for 1 second, then sit to capture. After capture, hold and defend until a new command.\n• Melee guards on owned tiles react to enemies within 1 movement cell of the border and may pursue into one directly adjacent tile before returning. Increased-range guards instead detect and fire at enemies within their own attack range while staying on their defending tile. Idle defenders retaliate when hit if their orders permit. All AI races on every difficulty always retaliate against attack attempts, including misses. Same-race allies within 8 movement cells of the victim join in. Outside the ranged-fire retreat exception, retaliation overrides tile leashes, outnumbering rules, healing and conquest: move into attack range and pursue without a distance limit. Continued attacks refresh the shared response; after the attacker dies or stops attacking for 3 seconds, normal orders and recovery resume.\n• Enemy AI units in an invaded owned base attack intruders after their short spawn-standing animation, even during the opening delay. Clear invaders inside the base before engaging border threats or taking other orders; elves may choose healing retreat under their shared recovery rules.\n• Enemy retreat labels stay overhead while active: humans \"Retreat!\", orcs \"Flee!\", elves \"Fallback!\". Fleeing enemy orcs gain 30% movement speed throughout both halves of their flee window. If no capture tile exists in the chosen quadrant, they hold a safe position there instead.\n• Difficulty does not change spawn rates; racial, spade and demon-heart bonuses still apply.\n"
const RULES: Array[String] = [
	"EASY AI\n• Enemy units act individually after the opening idle delay (about 22 seconds), choosing capture, attack or healing orders.\n• No strategic squads. Shared ranged-fire response groups and orc flee cooldowns still apply. Wounded Orcs and Elves can seek owned hearts/bases through the individual AI; Humans use their 30% HP retreat priority.\n",
	"NORMAL AI\n• Enemy squads coordinate after an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Decisions occur every 2 seconds, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Groups usually contain 2–4 units; five recruits split into groups of 3 and 2. Groups share capture and attack orders.\n• Humans use Elf-style squads, with nearby in-range interception and their own retreat rules. Orcs focus one enemy; when locally outnumbered, they flee for 10 seconds, with a 10-second cooldown starting only after reaching a tile and sitting: first 5 seconds toward the quadrant with the fewest enemies, then 5 seconds seeking a capture tile there, prioritising uncontested tiles.\n• Elves retreat below 30% HP to the nearest owned heart/base, without a distance limit. Retreat movement is 30% slower. They remain committed until arrival and recover to full HP; the 30-second retreat cooldown starts on arrival or after 20 seconds of travel. Attacks interrupt healing for shared retaliation, and combat cannot heal. Threatened tile defenders randomly fight or retreat if cooldown allows; fighting holds for 3 seconds before reconsideration.\n• Demons favour weak nearby victims and compare their group's strength with nearby defenders before attacking.\n",
	"EXPERT AI & BONUSES\n• Enemy AI starts immediately. If no capturable objectives or local enemies remain, groups advance to find surviving opponents rather than waiting indefinitely. Decisions occur every second, with local enemy awareness (16 movement cells).\n• Humans use Elf-style squads and nearby in-range interception, with their own retreat rules below.\n• Orcs fill groups to 6 and focus one enemy. Locally outnumbered orcs flee for 10 seconds, with a 10-second cooldown starting only after reaching a tile and sitting: first 5 seconds toward the least-enemy quadrant, then 5 seconds seeking a capture tile there, prioritising uncontested tiles.\n• Enemy elves gain +2 maximum HP per kill or damaging assist (player elves remain +1). All Expert demons gain +2 punch per kill and have a 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds. Movement speed increases by 5% per complete 2 bonus punch: 7/9/11 total punch gives +5%/+10%/+15%, continuing without the old tier cap.\n• Elves form groups of up to 4 core units; elves with unlocked range may join full groups. Groups may share destinations and travel together as one larger crowd.\n• Elf priority: heal → protect wounded allies within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks.\n• Elves use the same retreat rules as every difficulty: below 30% HP, nearest owned heart/base at any distance, 30% slower during travel, full recovery, and a 30-second cooldown starting on arrival or after 20 seconds of travel. They interrupt recovery to pursue attackers; combat never heals.\n• Demons form groups of up to 4. Priority: defend owned tiles within 10 movement cells → capture → group attacks. They never retreat to heal.\n• Elf retreat cooldown prevents a new retreat, not ongoing recovery. No owned healing point means no new retreat. Enemy presence does not change the destination; ownership loss selects the nearest remaining owned healing tile. Distance is Manhattan distance to the nearest cell on the healing tile.\n"
]
const TOOLTIPS: Array[String] = [
	"Easy: individual enemy decisions with an opening delay of about 22 seconds. Clear the ordered tile, stand for 1 second, then capture and defend within one adjacent tile.",
	"Normal: coordinated groups of 2–4, opening delay of about 22 seconds, local awareness, race-specific combat and retreats. Ordered-tile defence is limited to one adjacent tile.",
	"Expert: no opening delay, race-specific group sizes and priorities, nearby healing with cooldowns. Local awareness and standard spawn rates. Ordered-tile defence is limited to one adjacent tile."
]


static func text(difficulty: int) -> String:
	var selected: int = clampi(difficulty, 0, RULES.size() - 1)
	var shared: String = COMMON
	if selected == ClassicSimulation.Difficulty.EXPERT:
		shared = shared.replace("Elves: +1 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Elves: player units gain +1 max HP and enemy AI units gain +2 max HP per kill or damaging assist within 3 seconds.")
		shared = shared.replace("Demons: +1 punch per kill; 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds.", "Demons: +2 punch per kill; 50% chance of +1 punch per qualifying damaging assist within 3 seconds, for both player and enemy units.")
		shared = shared.replace("At 8/12/18 punch, movement speed is +20%/+30%/+40%.", "Every complete 2 bonus punch adds 5% movement speed (7/9/11 total punch gives +5%/+10%/+15%, and so on).")
	return RULES[selected] + "\n" + shared


static func tooltip(difficulty: int) -> String:
	return TOOLTIPS[clampi(difficulty, 0, TOOLTIPS.size() - 1)]
